            <ArticleTitle>Catheterization-documented coronary artery disease in young Chinese adults.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>301-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We conducted a retrospective study among 31 young (age&lt;40 years) Chinese patients with catheterization-documented coronary artery disease. Male gender and smoking were the most important risk factors. Most of them had a single or two-vessel coronary artery disease. Standard treatment strategies could be applied. The prognosis appeared to be excellent.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
